---
// Week 11 "See It": a guitar loudspeaker's structure (magnet, voice coil,
// cone, basket), and a simple two-frame sketch of why current direction
// sets motion direction — the coil sits in the magnet's field, so current
// through it creates a force that pushes the cone forward or pulls it
// back, depending on which way the current flows. Conceptual line
// sketches, not an accurate motor-structure or magnetic-field simulation.
---

<div class="speaker-diagrams">
  <figure class="speaker-card bench-module">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 200 110" role="img" aria-label="Cross section of a guitar loudspeaker: a magnet assembly with a gap holding the voice coil, the coil attached to a cone that widens toward the front, and sound radiating outward from the cone.">
      <rect x="14" y="34" width="22" height="42" class="magnet" />
      <rect x="36" y="42" width="10" height="26" class="pole-piece" />
      <rect x="48" y="46" width="10" height="18" class="coil" />
      <path d="M 46 46 L 46 64 M 50 46 L 50 64 M 54 46 L 54 64" class="coil-hatch" />
      <path d="M 58 55 L 84 55" class="former" />
      <path d="M 84 30 L 170 8 M 84 80 L 170 102" class="cone" />
      <path d="M 170 8 L 182 6 M 170 102 L 182 104" class="surround" />
      <path d="M 36 40 L 168 12 M 36 70 L 168 100" class="basket" stroke-dasharray="2 3" />
      <path d="M 190 40 Q 198 55 190 70" class="wave" fill="none" />
      <path d="M 198 34 Q 208 55 198 76" class="wave" fill="none" />
      <line x1="52" y1="88" x2="80" y2="88" class="motion-line" />
      <path d="M 68 84 L 80 88 L 68 92 M 64 84 L 52 88 L 64 92" class="motion-arrow" fill="none" />
      <text x="25" y="30" class="part-label" text-anchor="middle">magnet</text>
      <text x="53" y="40" class="part-label" text-anchor="middle">voice coil</text>
      <text x="125" y="6" class="part-label" text-anchor="middle">cone</text>
      <text x="66" y="100" class="part-label" text-anchor="middle">motion</text>
      <text x="200" y="20" class="part-label" text-anchor="middle">radiated sound</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>
      <span class="speaker-label">Loudspeaker structure</span>
      <span class="speaker-description">A voice coil sits in a magnet's fixed field and is attached to a cone. Current through the coil creates a force that moves the coil and cone together, and that mechanical motion is what pushes on the surrounding air.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <figure class="speaker-card bench-module">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 200 100" role="img" aria-label="Two frames showing that reversing the direction of current through the voice coil reverses the direction the cone moves: current one way pushes the cone forward, current the other way pulls it back.">
      <g>
        <rect x="10" y="38" width="16" height="24" class="coil" />
        <path d="M 8 30 L 20 30" class="wire" />
        <path d="M 16 26 L 20 30 L 16 34" class="wire" fill="none" />
        <path d="M 30 50 L 62 38" class="cone" />
        <path d="M 30 50 L 62 62" class="cone" />
        <text x="18" y="20" class="part-label" text-anchor="middle">current →</text>
        <text x="46" y="80" class="part-label" text-anchor="middle">cone pushed forward</text>
      </g>
      <g transform="translate(100, 0)">
        <rect x="10" y="38" width="16" height="24" class="coil" />
        <path d="M 20 30 L 8 30" class="wire" />
        <path d="M 12 26 L 8 30 L 12 34" class="wire" fill="none" />
        <path d="M 30 50 L 58 42" class="cone" />
        <path d="M 30 50 L 58 58" class="cone" />
        <text x="18" y="20" class="part-label" text-anchor="middle">current ←</text>
        <text x="44" y="80" class="part-label" text-anchor="middle">cone pulled back</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>
      <span class="speaker-label">Current direction sets motion direction</span>
      <span class="speaker-description">Reversing the current through the voice coil reverses the force on it, so the cone moves the other way — this back-and-forth motion, driven directly by the amplifier's electrical signal, is what produces sound.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>

<style>
  .speaker-diagrams {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .speaker-card {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .speaker-card svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .magnet {
    fill: var(--at-bg-alt);
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .pole-piece {
    fill: var(--at-bg);
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .coil {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--at-accent);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .coil-hatch {
    stroke: var(--at-accent);
    stroke-width: 1;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .former {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    fill: none;
  }

  .cone {
    stroke: var(--bench-phosphor, var(--at-accent));
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    fill: none;
  }

  .surround {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    fill: none;
  }

  .basket {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1;
    fill: none;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .wave {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .motion-line {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1;
    stroke-dasharray: 2 2;
  }

  .motion-arrow {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1.2;
  }

  .wire {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    fill: none;
  }

  .part-label {
    font-family: var(--bench-readout, var(--at-font-mono));
    font-size: 6px;
    fill: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }

  figcaption {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }

  .speaker-label {
    font-family: var(--bench-readout, var(--at-font-mono));
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--at-text);
  }

  .speaker-description {
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-xs);
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
</style>
